  "body": "Release 0.9.0 of cedar-policy-symcc, available on crates.io.\r\n\r\nChanges in this release:\r\n- Faster symbolic compilation. Queries now produce smaller footprints, because terms with a constant value are dropped and `in` only contributes its left operand. This means fewer transitivity and acyclicity constraints, a lot fewer on some queries (#2708, #2709). There is also less work on trivial transitivity constraints (#2703) and quicker term comparisons (#2595).\r\n- Set literals are now encoded as a set.union of singletons instead of nested set.insert (#2717). The generated SMT changes, but verification results are the same."
